---
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400.css';
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400-italic.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/500.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/600.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/500.css';
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import CaffeineDay from '../../../components/coffee/CaffeineDay.svelte';
import { METHODS, CAFFEINE, GUIDANCE, SOURCES, buildRecipe, estimateBrewedMg, espressoMg, flOzToMl } from '../../../lib/coffee/index.ts';

const title = 'Caffeine Calculator: How Much Is Still in You at Bedtime';
const description = 'Add the coffees you drink and see your caffeine total for the day and how much is still in your body at bedtime, with caffeine by brew method, espresso shot and cup size.';

// Caffeine in an 8 oz cup by method, at the Brew Guide's classic ratio (arabica).
const eightOz = flOzToMl(8);
const rows = METHODS.filter((m) => !['espresso', 'moka', 'cold-brew'].includes(m.id)).map((m) => {
	const r = buildRecipe({ method: m.id, target: { cupMl: eightOz } });
	const dose = r.ok ? r.value.doseG : eightOz / 14;
	const mg = estimateBrewedMg(dose, m.id);
	return { label: m.label, dose, mg: mg.ok ? mg.value : null };
});
const cold = (() => { const r = buildRecipe({ method: 'cold-brew', target: { cupMl: flOzToMl(16) } }); const mg = r.ok ? estimateBrewedMg(r.value.doseG, 'cold-brew') : null; return mg && mg.ok ? mg.value : null; })();
const single = espressoMg(1), double = espressoMg(2);
const fmt = (r: { min: number; max: number } | null) => (r ? `${Math.round(r.min / 5) * 5}–${Math.round(r.max / 5) * 5} mg` : '—');
const fda = GUIDANCE.find((g) => g.id === 'fda-adult-daily')!;
const acog = GUIDANCE.find((g) => g.id === 'acog-pregnancy')!;
const efsa = GUIDANCE.find((g) => g.id === 'efsa-single-dose')!;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			'@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'Caffeine Calculator',
			url: 'https://jayarr.coffee/tools/caffeine/', description, applicationCategory: 'HealthApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any',
			offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
			publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'JayArr Coffee', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee' },
		})}></script>
	</head>
	<body class="cf-page">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="cf-intro">
				<a href="/tools/" class="cf-back">← All tools</a>
				<p class="cf-kicker">Caffeine Calculator</p>
				<h1>How much caffeine is <em>still in you at bedtime?</em></h1>
				<p class="cf-lede">Add what you drink and when. You see today's total, and a curve of how much caffeine is in your body hour by hour, falling by half roughly every five hours.</p>
			</section>
			<section class="cf-tool" aria-label="Caffeine Calculator"><CaffeineDay client:load /></section>

			<article class="cf-body">
				<h2>How much caffeine is in a cup of coffee?</h2>
				<p>It depends mostly on how much coffee went into the cup. A typical 8 oz cup brewed at a 1:16 ratio uses about 15–17 g of coffee, and arabica beans are roughly 1% caffeine by weight, most of which ends up in the cup. That puts most home-brewed 8 oz cups at about 100–200 mg. Robusta beans carry roughly twice the caffeine.</p>
				<div class="cf-table-wrap">
					<table>
						<thead><tr><th scope="col">Drink</th><th scope="col">Serving</th><th scope="col">Caffeine (estimate)</th></tr></thead>
						<tbody>
							{rows.map((r) => <tr><th scope="row">{r.label}</th><td>8 oz, {Math.round(r.dose)} g coffee</td><td>{fmt(r.mg)}</td></tr>)}
							<tr><th scope="row">Cold brew</th><td>16 oz, diluted 1:1</td><td>{fmt(cold)}</td></tr>
							<tr><th scope="row">Espresso</th><td>single shot (about 1 oz)</td><td>{fmt(single)}</td></tr>
							<tr><th scope="row">Double espresso, latte or cappuccino</th><td>two shots</td><td>{fmt(double)}</td></tr>
							<tr><th scope="row">Decaf</th><td>6 oz</td><td>{CAFFEINE.decafPer6Oz.min}–{CAFFEINE.decafPer6Oz.max} mg</td></tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
				<p class="cf-note">Estimates for arabica at the Brew Guide's classic ratios; a stronger ratio or robusta beans push them up. Café cups are often larger and stronger.</p>

				<h2>Does espresso have more caffeine than drip coffee?</h2>
				<p>Per sip, yes; per drink, usually not. A single shot holds about {CAFFEINE.espressoShotMg.typical} mg in about an ounce, so it is far more concentrated, but an 8 oz cup of drip coffee carries more in total. A latte or cappuccino made with a double shot lands near {Math.round(double.min)}–{Math.round(double.max)} mg, close to a cup of drip.</p>

				<h2>How long caffeine stays in your body</h2>
				<p>The body clears caffeine at a steady proportional rate: on average, half of it is gone after about five hours, but that half-life ranges from about 1.5 to 10 hours between people. Smoking speeds it up; pregnancy and oral contraceptives slow it down, and late in pregnancy it can take up to three times longer. A 200 mg coffee at 3 pm can leave around 100 mg in you at 8 pm and around 50 mg near 1 am, which is why an afternoon coffee can still matter at bedtime.</p>
				<p>The calculator draws that curve for your day. It also allows for about 45 minutes for caffeine to be absorbed, so each drink rises before it falls. It is an illustration of the average pattern, not a measurement of your body.</p>

				<h2>How much is too much?</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Most adults:</strong> {fda.wording}</li>
					<li><strong>In one go:</strong> {efsa.wording}</li>
					<li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> {acog.wording}</li>
				</ul>
				<p>These are general figures. Sensitivity varies a lot, and some medicines and conditions change it; ask a doctor about your own case.</p>

				<h2>Related guides</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><a href="/blog/caffeine-in-coffee-guide/">Caffeine in coffee: a complete guide</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/how-is-coffee-decaffeinated/">How coffee is decaffeinated</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/whats-different-about-ristretto-or-lungo-espresso-shots/">Ristretto and lungo shots</a></li>
					<li><a href="/tools/brew-ratio/">Brew Guide: coffee, water and timing for any brewer</a></li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Sources</h2>
				<ul class="cf-sources">
					<li>{SOURCES['newcastle-2018'].author}, <cite>{SOURCES['newcastle-2018'].title}</cite> ({SOURCES['newcastle-2018'].year}).</li>
					<li>U.S. Food and Drug Administration, <cite>Spilling the Beans: How Much Caffeine is Too Much?</cite>, consumer update, content current as of August 28, 2024; European Food Safety Authority, scientific opinion on the safety of caffeine (2015); American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists, <cite>Committee Opinion No. 462: Moderate Caffeine Consumption During Pregnancy</cite> (2010, reaffirmed).</li>
					<li>{SOURCES.synthesis.author}, <cite>{SOURCES.synthesis.title}</cite>: §15 caffeine metabolism and half-life, §17 caffeine by brew method.</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>.cf-page { background: #f3ede3; }</style>
<style>
	main { color: #2a1d15; }
	.cf-intro { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px 22px; }
	.cf-back { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; text-decoration: none; }
	.cf-kicker { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8f5d22; margin: 26px 0 0; }
	h1 { font: 400 clamp(40px, 6vw, 68px)/.98 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 10px 0 12px; }
	h1 em { font-style: italic; color: #7a4e30; }
	.cf-lede { font: 400 17px/1.5 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; color: #5b4a3d; max-width: 60ch; margin: 0; }
	.cf-tool { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8px 24px 40px; }
	.cf-body { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 24px 72px; font: 400 17px/1.7 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; }
	.cf-body h2 { font: 400 34px/1.1 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; margin: 44px 0 12px; }
	.cf-body a { color: #7a4e30; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
	.cf-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid #d9cdbd; border-radius: 12px; background: #fbf8f3; }
	table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 15px; }
	th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e6dccd; }
	thead th { font: 500 11px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; }
	td { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; }
	tr:last-child th, tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
	.cf-note, .cf-sources { font-size: 14.5px; color: #5b4a3d; }
	@media (max-width: 640px) { .cf-intro { padding: 96px 16px 18px; } .cf-tool { padding: 4px 12px 32px; } .cf-body { padding: 16px 16px 56px; } }
</style>
